+Author: Pirmin Vogel <vogelpi@lowrisc.org>
+Date:   Thu Jan 9 17:26:40 2025 +0100

-    [aes, pre-dv] Remove test vector redundancies
+    [aes/rtl] Correct manual operation mode for GCM

-    Firstly, this commit removes some redundant instructions in the test
-    vector sequences, e.g., unnecessary writes to the `CTRL_GCM` register.
-    Secondly, some redundant polls for the `IDLE` bit in the `STATUS`
-    register are replaced with polls for the `INPUT_READY` bit.
+    This commit cleans up the generation of GCM specific start signals
+    and properly handles manual operation mode for GCM. Previously, some
+    GCM phases (especially the ones not using the AES cipher core) would
+    start automatically despite the module being configured in manual
+    operation mode.

-    Signed-off-by: Andrea Caforio <andrea.caforio@lowrisc.org>
+    Signed-off-by: Pirmin Vogel <vogelpi@lowrisc.org>
